  {
   "id": "7_6ZfquwAwAJ",
   "from": "Eric Innocents EBOULET",
   "author": "31dc03607958a62a",
   "date": "2016-10-29T18:30:06Z",
   "subject": "Re: Discrete Variable Conditional on Continuous Variable: How to Fit in Stan? (Exponential Distribution)",
   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\">Hi, you can read also chapter 12 in the stands manuel.<div><br></div><div>Bests regard</div></div>"
    ],
    [
     3,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><div><br><br>Le samedi 29 octobre 2016 02:39:51 UTC+2, Dalton Hance a écrit :<blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0;margin-left:0.8ex;border-left:1px #ccc solid;padding-left:1ex\"><div dir=\"ltr\">I guess I&#39;ll take the opportunity to answer my own question. I had a coding error when trying to implement the indicator variable for when arrival time is observed. Below is the corrected code which returns reasonable result matching the JAGS output.<div><br></div><div><div style=\"background-color:rgb(250,250,250);border-color:rgb(187,187,187);border-style:solid;border-width:1px;word-wrap:break-word\"><code><div><span style=\"color:#000\">stan_proof_of_concept </span><span style=\"color:#660\">&lt;-</span><span style=\"color:#080\">&quot;<br>data {<br>  int&lt;lower = 0&gt; N_obs;<br>  int&lt;lower = 0&gt; N_mis;<br>  real&lt;lower =0&gt; y_obs[N_obs];<br>}<br><br><br>parameters {<br>  real&lt;lower = 0&gt; rate;<br>  real&lt;lower = 0, upper = 1&gt; p[2];<br>}<br><br><br>model {<br>  for(i in 1:N_mis)<br>    target += log_sum_exp(log1m(p[1]) + exponential_lcdf(1|rate),<br>                          log1m(p[2]) + exponential_lccdf(1|rate));<br><br><br>  for (i in 1:N_obs) {<br>    if (y_obs[i] &lt;= 1) {<br>      target += log(p[1]) + exponential_lpdf(y_obs[i]|rate);<br>    } else {<br>      target += log(p[2]) + exponential_lpdf(y_obs[i]|rate);<br>    }<br>  }<br>}<br>&quot;</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br></span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br></span></div></code></div><div><br><br></div><div><div><br>On Friday, October 28, 2016 at 3:28:08 PM UTC-7, Dalton Hance wrote:<blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0;margin-left:0.8ex;border-left:1px #ccc solid;padding-left:1ex\"><div dir=\"ltr\">I&#39;m trying to wrap my head around a toy example for a much harder problem. I&#39;m interested in modelling the probability of detection of some event conditional on the arrival time of that event. As an example I&#39;m using the exponential distribution. Let the arrival time of the i^th event be distributed as exponential with some rate parameter, lambda. If the arrival time is less than 1, the event is detected with probability p_1; and if the arrival time is greater than 1, the event is detect with with probability p_2. &quot;Detection&quot; is probably the wrong word here though. Because I am assuming that if an event is not detected, we know that it occurred, but we don&#39;t the arrival time. In other words, given that arrival time is less than 1 we record a zero with probability (1-p_1) and if arrival time is greater than 1 we record a zero with probability (1-p_2).<div><br></div><div>This is easily simulated in R as follows:</div><div><br></div><div><div style=\"background-color:rgb(250,250,250);border-color:rgb(187,187,187);border-style:solid;border-width:1px;word-wrap:break-word\"><code><div><span style=\"color:#000\">y </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> rexp</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#066\">1000</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br></span><span style=\"color:#008\">set</span><span style=\"color:#660\">.</span><span style=\"color:#000\">seed</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#066\">36</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>p </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> plogis</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">rnorm</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#066\">2</span><span style=\"color:#660\">))</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br><br><br>x </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> rep</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">NA</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#066\">1000</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>z </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> rep</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">NA</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#066\">1000</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br><br><br></span><span style=\"color:#008\">for</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">i </span><span style=\"color:#008\">in</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#066\">1</span><span style=\"color:#660\">:</span><span style=\"color:#066\">1000</span><span style=\"color:#660\">){</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>  x</span><span style=\"color:#660\">[</span><span style=\"color:#000\">i</span><span style=\"color:#660\">]</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> rbinom</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#066\">1</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#066\">1</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> p</span><span style=\"color:#660\">[(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">y</span><span style=\"color:#660\">[</span><span style=\"color:#000\">i</span><span style=\"color:#660\">]</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">&gt;</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#066\">1</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">+</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#066\">1</span><span style=\"color:#660\">])</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>  z</span><span style=\"color:#660\">[</span><span style=\"color:#000\">i</span><span style=\"color:#660\">]</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> x</span><span style=\"color:#660\">[</span><span style=\"color:#000\">i</span><span style=\"color:#660\">]*</span><span style=\"color:#000\">y</span><span style=\"color:#660\">[</span><span style=\"color:#000\">i</span><span style=\"color:#660\">]</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br></span><span style=\"color:#660\">}</span></div></code></div><div><br></div><div>As a proof of concept I can fit this model in JAGS as follows:<br></div></div><div><br></div><div><div style=\"background-color:rgb(250,250,250);border-color:rgb(187,187,187);border-style:solid;border-width:1px;word-wrap:break-word\"><code><div><span style=\"color:#000\">library</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">rjags</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br><br>jags_proof_of_concept </span><span style=\"color:#660\">&lt;-</span><span style=\"color:#080\">&quot;<br>model{<br>  for (i in 1:N) {<br>      y[i] ~ dexp(rate)<br>      x[i] ~ dbern(ifelse(y[i] &lt;= 1, p[1], p[2]))<br>  }<br>  p[1] ~ dbeta(1,1)<br>  p[2] ~ dbeta(1,1)<br>  rate ~ dgamma(.01,.01)<br>}&quot;</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br><br>jags_POC </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> jags</span><span style=\"color:#660\">.</span><span style=\"color:#000\">model</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">textConnection</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\"><span style=\"color:#000\">jags_proof_of_concept</span></span><span style=\"color:#660\">),</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> <br>                  data </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> list</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">N </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> length</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">x</span><span style=\"color:#660\">),</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>                              x </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> x</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>                              y </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> ifelse</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">x </span><span style=\"color:#660\">==</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#066\">0</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> NA</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> y</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)),</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>                  n</span><span style=\"color:#660\">.</span><span style=\"color:#000\">chains </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#066\">4</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>                  n</span><span style=\"color:#660\">.</span><span style=\"color:#000\">adapt  </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#066\">1000</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>                  </span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br><br>jags_out </span><span style=\"color:#660\">&lt;-</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> coda</span><span style=\"color:#660\">.</span><span style=\"color:#000\">samples</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">model</span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\">jags_POC</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>            variable</span><span style=\"color:#660\">.</span><span style=\"color:#000\">names</span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\">c</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#080\">&quot;rate&quot;</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#080\">&quot;p&quot;</span><span styl